			<div class="content" id="post-content-4148605">
									

<p>Not a terrible concept. Execution could use a lot of improvement, but not terrible. I'm pleased that you addressed the question of what happens if the culprit doesn't have any money.</p>
<p>'Trehiog' notion is dreadful, though. And if this thing only activates for <em>insults</em>, why would it go after <em>swear words</em> by themselves?</p>
<p>does a sincere &quot;that's fucking brilliant!&quot; activate it?</p>
<p>does &quot;son of a bitch, i just stepped in dog shit&quot; activate it?</p>
<p>and the test with Dr Martens is completely broken. First it punishes people for using insults, then it punishes someone for <em>not</em> using insults? I understand that you're trying to imply that it decided he's being passive-aggressive, but is there any way to satisfy this thing?</p>
<p>What about indirect insults? &quot;You're much more intelligent than I expected from someone of your ethnic group! And I expected you'd smell terrible, but you don't!&quot;</p>
<p>What about the types of ambiguous insults where there's a perfectly plausible alternate interpretation? e.g., the employer reference letter joke &quot;you'll be very lucky if this man works for you&quot; ?</p>
<p>edit: or statements of fact - &quot;I don't like you&quot; ? &quot;You've repeatedly made serious mistakes, despite having lots of patient assistance, to the extent that I'm forced to question your basic competence&quot; ?</p>

							</div>

								
